# CODEOWNERS — human review required for Foundation (PRODUCT_CANON C-29/C-30).
#
# Foundation is the deployment-independent machinery: schemas, state machines,
# security boundaries, providers, installers, migrations and the control plane.
# It changes only through a reviewed platform release, never from a deployment.
# Fleet Definition content (roles, soul overlays, declarative skills, processes,
# responsibilities, policies) is the *other* loop — it is authored by Prime in the
# tenant registry and does not pass through this file at all.
#
# This list previously covered three paths (.github, contracts.json, daemon/),
# leaving the brain, libs, system tooling, manifests, bootstrap scripts, skills
# and the entire dashboard unowned.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IF YOU FORKED THIS TEMPLATE: replace the owner below with a team or user in
# YOUR organisation that has write access.
#
# An owner that does not resolve is not a weaker rule — GitHub ignores it, so
# the rule stops existing while still reading like one. With "require review
# from Code Owners" enabled, that leaves protection configured and unenforced,
# which is the worst of the available states. The `CODEOWNERS Resolves` CI job
# fails on exactly this, so a fork finds out on its first push rather than on
# the first unreviewed merge.
#
# Every rule below names the same owner, so the path list adds no enforcement
# over the `*` line — it is documentation of what counts as Foundation, and the
# authoritative version of that list lives in docs/MODULE_CHARTER.md and is
# enforced by test/boundaries.test.mjs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

